0.9.17
- when classifying species as unambiguous, ambiguous or synonym, a type strain representative also anchors its reference and NCBI species if these differ from the species it is type material of and no type strain genome of these species is a representative (e.g. s__Mycobacteroides abscessus for G000069185, in the type strains ledger as s__Mycobacterium abscessus)
- no error is logged when the species names of a type strain representative are all assigned to its cluster

0.9.16
- species names that keep the previous placeholder specific name (RETAIN_PREVIOUS_PLACEHOLDER_NAME) separate the generic and specific names with a space instead of an underscore

0.9.15
- pmc_species_names and u_pmc_species_names name SeqCode type genomes by the type species and type strain rules, using the species genomes are type material of (GTDB type strains ledger, else SeqCode, else NCBI), instead of a separate SeqCode step that ignored the ledgers, untrustworthy type material, gender agreement and the type species genus check
- species are classified as unambiguous, ambiguous or synonym by the species type strain genomes are type material of and the reference (SeqCode or NCBI) species of other genomes; SeqCode names are valid names in priority checks; final_taxonomy_metadata.tsv, gtdb_sp_clusters.ncbi_sp.tsv and species_classification_ledger_updates.tsv gain SeqCode columns
- gtdb_synonyms_final.tsv has a header for the reference species columns of synonyms.tsv

0.9.14
- u_species_init names species clusters from the species their type material is type material of (GTDB type strains ledger, else SeqCode, else NCBI) and other clusters from their reference (SeqCode or NCBI) binomial, so SeqCode-named clusters are named at initialisation; type species of genus genomes without a species name are logged as warnings instead of stopping the step
- new genomes with a previously unseen SeqCode or NCBI species take that genus and species instead of the GTDB-Tk classification
- SeqCode names are valid names and the SeqCode year of the type species is the year of priority of genera without an LPSN entry; name and curation logs gain SeqCode species, genus and reference source columns, and conflicting_type_species_of_genus.tsv gains a reference source column and is sorted

0.9.13
- u_curation_trees identifies new taxa from the reference (SeqCode or NCBI) classification of genomes in the previous and current release, so new SeqCode taxa are placed in the curation trees; tables gain a reference source column and tables and trees are written in sorted order

0.9.12
- u_synonyms counts names validly published under the SeqCode as valid names when checking the priority of synonyms, so SeqCode-named representatives are no longer reported as having incorrect priority

0.9.11
- u_synonyms identifies type strain synonyms by the species genomes are type material of (GTDB type strains ledger, else SeqCode, else NCBI) and majority vote synonyms by the reference (SeqCode or NCBI) species, so SeqCode type genomes take part under their SeqCode name; synonyms.tsv gains reference species and source columns for the representative and synonym, which are read in preference to the NCBI species columns, and rows without a species name are skipped when read

0.9.10
- u_ncbi_erroneous: type strain genomes also anchor their NCBI species when it differs from the species they are type material of and has no other type strain genome, so genomes assigned to an NCBI species whose type genome was renamed under the SeqCode are still reported as misclassified

0.9.9
- u_ncbi_erroneous groups genomes by their reference (SeqCode or NCBI) species and anchors each species by the type strain genomes of that species (GTDB type strains ledger, else SeqCode, else NCBI), so SeqCode type genomes anchor their SeqCode name; the misclassified genomes table gains SeqCode species, SeqCode genus and reference source columns; ledger warnings name every metadata file when the metadata is split by domain

0.9.8
- u_cluster_named_reps, u_cluster_de_novo and u_cluster_stats report the reference (SeqCode or NCBI) species of representatives: cluster and ANI radius tables gain SeqCode species, SeqCode genus and reference source columns, and the E. coli/Shigella type strain check uses the reference species

0.9.7
- u_sel_reps identifies named species and their type material by the reference (SeqCode or NCBI) species of genomes, so SeqCode species without an NCBI name get a representative selected under their SeqCode name; names validly published under the SeqCode count as valid names when resolving close ANI neighbours; tables gain SeqCode species, SeqCode genus and reference source columns

0.9.6
- Ctrl-C now stops all skani pool workers: workers ignore SIGINT and the main process terminates the pool when interrupted, so no orphaned workers (and .nfs files in the output directory) are left behind

0.9.5
- The year of priority of a name validly published under both the ICNP (LPSN) and the SeqCode is the earlier of the two (SeqCode Rule 23c); SeqCode type genomes with no LPSN year use their SeqCode year
- Species priority uses the reference (SeqCode or NCBI) species of genomes, and names validly published under the SeqCode count as valid names
- u_rep_actions groups type strain genomes by the species they are type material of when checking naming priority, and its tables gain SeqCode species, SeqCode genus and reference source columns

0.9.4
- u_rep_changes compares the reference (SeqCode or NCBI) species of previous representatives between releases, so a representative whose SeqCode name is unchanged is not reported as reassigned when its NCBI species changes; rep_change_summary.tsv gains SeqCode species, SeqCode genus and reference source columns

0.9.3
- u_resolve_types groups type strain genomes by the species they are type material of (GTDB type strains ledger, then SeqCode, then NCBI), so SeqCode type genomes are checked for conflicting type material; a genome that is the type genome of a SeqCode species counts as type material at its source; tables gain SeqCode species, SeqCode genus and reference source columns
- A GTDB type strains ledger entry is only reported as redundant when it also leaves the GTDB species unchanged

0.9.2
- u_lpsn_rna_types also matches LPSN type 16S rRNA sequences to genomes under their SeqCode species, and reports SeqCode species, SeqCode genus and reference source columns
- Plan: the year of priority of a name validly published under both the SeqCode and LPSN will be the earlier of the two (SeqCode Rule 23c); applied from the u_rep_actions PR

0.9.1
- u_qc_genomes groups genomes by their reference (SeqCode or NCBI) species when checking that each named species retains a type genome, and its tables gain SeqCode species, SeqCode genus and reference source columns

0.9.0
- Genomes carry their SeqCode taxonomy (Genome.seqcode_taxa) read from the SeqCode table; Genome.ref_taxa resolves to the SeqCode taxonomy when present and the NCBI taxonomy otherwise, and Genome.type_species() gives the species a type genome is type material of (GTDB type strains ledger, then ref_taxa)
- All u_* commands load the SeqCode table for the previous and current genome sets; loading warns when the table and metadata disagree and when a type strains ledger entry conflicts with SeqCode or is redundant
- No command reads the new fields yet, so outputs are unchanged (see docs/seqcode_taxonomy_plan.md)

0.8.11
- u_synonyms identifies majority vote synonyms in a single pass over NCBI species instead of comparing each NCBI species to every GTDB species cluster

0.8.10
- u_cluster_de_novo reports the number of genomes that could not be assigned to the closest representative within its ANI radius
- Faster loading of genome sets: NCBI assembly files are read once and cached, and taxonomy strings are parsed once

0.8.9
- u_resolve_types does not consider a type strain genome with a conflicting LTP 16S rRNA assignment untrustworthy if it meets the strain ANI criterion with a retained type strain genome that has the expected LTP assignment

0.8.8
- u_rep_changes checks whether a species cluster with a lost representative is in the disband_cluster_ledger, and writes all columns of rep_change_summary.tsv for these clusters
- u_rep_actions disbands clusters before replacing lost representatives, so a disbanded cluster with a lost representative is not given a new representative
- u_rep_actions does not select a Shigella genome as the representative when checking naming priority

0.8.7
- u_rep_changes, u_rep_actions, u_cluster_named_reps and u_cluster_de_novo load the ncbi_untrustworthy_sp_ledger, so genomes with an untrustworthy NCBI species assignment are not treated as type strains when representatives are selected; previously only u_sel_reps and later steps loaded this ledger

0.8.6
- u_rep_actions never selects a genome from a Shigella species as a replacement representative, as these species are synonyms of E. coli under the GTDB; a species cluster with no other genomes is retired
- u_cluster_named_reps and u_cluster_de_novo log an error unless all E. coli and Shigella type strain genomes are in a single species cluster that is not represented by a Shigella genome
- the Shigella species ignored by u_sel_reps are defined once in defaults.py

0.8.5
- u_cluster_de_novo compares each genome only against the representatives it has a skani hit with when assigning genomes to representatives and when greedily selecting de novo representatives, instead of against every representative; results are identical and the assignment step takes seconds instead of ~20 hours on R237
- u_cluster_de_novo progress lines are updated every 1,000 genomes

0.8.4
- fixed u_synonyms and u_species_init failing with a TypeError because NCBI_SpeciesManager was not passed the untrustworthy type material file
- genomes considered untrustworthy as type material are now ignored when checking that all type strain genomes of an NCBI species are in a single GTDB cluster
- u_ncbi_erroneous treats genomes in the GTDB type strains ledger as type strains of the ledger species, matching u_resolve_types; they anchor their NCBI species only if it has no other type strain genomes

0.8.3
- the ambiguous_sp_priority.tsv file lists each pair of species once, instead of listing a pair as both A vs B and B vs A

0.8.2
- u_rep_actions calculates ANI between representatives and the genomes in their species clusters for all species in a single parallel batch, instead of one species at a time, when identifying improved representatives and replacing NCBI anomalous assemblies; this uses all specified CPUs (~8x faster with 32 CPUs in testing)

0.8.1
- the ncbi_env_bioproject_ledger now has an `Assembly type` column of `Environmental` or `Isolates`; only Environmental BioProjects are treated as MAGs/SAGs when genomes are loaded
- u_rep_actions no longer warns about BioProjects marked as Isolates replacing representatives with presumed isolates
- processing stops if the ledger lacks the `Assembly type` column or has another assembly type

0.8.0
- u_resolve_types groups genomes in the GTDB type strains ledger with the type strain genomes of their ledger species instead of their NCBI species
- in species with a genome in the GTDB type strains ledger, other type strain genomes are untrustworthy unless they have >=99% ANI to a ledger genome; ledger genomes are never considered untrustworthy (including for being `not used as type` at NCBI)
- u_resolve_types stops with an error if a genome is in both the GTDB type strains ledger and the untrustworthy type ledger
- u_rep_changes considers the NCBI species of genomes in the GTDB type strains ledger to be unchanged since the ledger species overrides the NCBI species

0.7.9
