- NCBI `assembly from heterotypic synonym type material` is now recognized as synonym type material (in addition to `assembly from synonym type material`, which NCBI no longer uses), so these genomes are considered type strains of subspecies or synonyms

0.7.8
- u_resolve_types only warns that an untrustworthy type genome conflicts with high-confidence LTP 16S rRNA assignments when a retained type genome has a conflicting LTP assignment; genomes already marked untrustworthy are no longer considered
- the warning now names the NCBI species and the retained genomes with conflicting LTP assignments
- in species resolved by u_resolve_types, retained type genomes whose high-confidence LTP 16S rRNA hits are all to other species are considered untrustworthy if another retained type genome has a hit to the expected species; genomes in the GTDB type strains ledger are exempt

0.7.7
- u_resolve_types lightly cleans LTP taxonomy strings: type material and strain information are split off at the last '|', and surrounding whitespace and leading or trailing '|' or '.' characters are removed from each taxon
- this allows LTP entries such as Oxalobacter paeniformigenes (JAMKYL010000000) to be parsed and removes trailing spaces from 7 LTP species names
- u_resolve_types writes LTP sequences without a valid taxonomy string (e.g. ';;|') to ltp_missing_taxonomy.tsv instead of logging a warning for each

0.7.6
- u_lpsn_rna_types warns when a genome with the LPSN type 16S rRNA gene is in the untrustworthy type ledger, and notes this in a new Notes column of lpsn_ssu_type_genomes.tsv
- u_lpsn_rna_types no longer counts genomes untrustworthy as type among those to add to the gtdb_type_strains ledger

